# Tunnel settings for scripts/start-with-tunnel.sh (deno task start:tunnel).
# Copy to .env.tunnel (gitignored) and fill in ONE option below.
# The environment wins over this file (e.g. TUNNEL_NAME= deno task start:tunnel
# ignores the file's TUNNEL_NAME). Nothing set → quick tunnel (URL changes on
# every restart). If the named tunnel fails its health check, the script falls
# back to a quick tunnel with a loud warning.

# Option A: locally managed named tunnel (native cloudflared).
# One-time setup: see README → Before the course.
TUNNEL_NAME=qwuo
PUBLIC_URL=https://quiz.example.com
# Optional: the credentials JSON from `cloudflared tunnel create`
# (default: cloudflared finds ~/.cloudflared/<tunnel-id>.json).
# TUNNEL_CRED_FILE=/Users/you/.cloudflared/<tunnel-id>.json

# Option B: dashboard tunnel token (Docker or native). Secret: never commit it.
# Public hostname service in the dashboard: http://localhost:3001 (native)
# or http://host.docker.internal:3001 (Docker).
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=<token from Zero Trust → Networks → Tunnels>
# PUBLIC_URL=https://quiz.example.com
